  id: Right_Lobe
  partName: Right Lobe
  descriptionChunks:
  - The right lobe is the largest division of the liver and plays a dominant role
    in its metabolic, synthetic, and detoxification activities. It processes nutrients
    absorbed from the digestive system, produces essential plasma proteins, and filters
    toxins from the blood.
  - This lobe contains a dense network of hepatic cells supported by a rich vascular
    supply, enabling high-volume metabolic throughput. Its proper function is critical
    for maintaining blood chemistry, supporting digestion through bile production,
    and regulating the body's chemical environment.
